** ============================================================
** BOUNDARY CONDITIONS
** ============================================================
**
** VARIANT: FREE BOUNDARIES. Only the RIGHT concrete face (x = +slab_w/2, the
** face the plate is pushed towards) is fully fixed. The LEFT (x = -slab_w/2),
** BACK (z = -slab_w/2) and BOTTOM (y = -slab_h) faces are left FREE, so the
** slab is supported only by the right face and the z-symmetry plane. The
** original models fix all four faces.
*Boundary
concrete-1.right,  1, 1
concrete-1.right,  2, 2
concrete-1.right,  3, 3
** left / back / bottom: free (deliberately no *Boundary)

** Symmetry boundary conditions in Z-direction
*Boundary
steel-1.z_symm, zSYMM
concrete-1.z_symm, zSYMM

** Loading node sets on the plate LEFT face (x = -plate_w/2), defined in
** mesh/steel.inp at four heights (h = tPlate = 20 mm):
**   plate_left_h0      y = 0        plate bottom (concrete surface)
**   plate_left_h1_3    y = h/3      == plate_left_loading (reference case)
**   plate_left_h2_3    y = 2h/3
**   plate_left_h1      y = h        plate top
** To load at another height replace plate_left_loading by the wanted set
** HERE and in the loading step below. fileOutput.inc already writes RF
** for all four sets.
**
** Fix plate movement in X-direction except where loaded
steel-1.plate_left_loading, 1, 1

